# Savefiles that are known not to load, and why.
#
# One "name: reason" a line; '#' comments. The suite treats a listed file's
# refusal as expected, and also fails if a listed file *loads* -- a manifest
# that outlives its reason would silently excuse the next real break.
#
# Take an entry out when the file loads again, rather than leaving it here.

# DEC-50, 2 September 2026: the Life realm took Zangband's four prayer books in
# place of Angband's five, and a book's object kind is created by its book: line
# in class.txt. A savefile names an object by tval and sval *as text*, so the
# moment [Novice's Handbook] stopped existing, every save holding one stopped
# being readable -- and every save holds one, because every save carries the
# town temple's stock and the temple sells prayer books.
#
# Measured before the change, not after: the two town prayer books appear in 35
# of 35 of these files; the three dungeon books in 0, 1 and 1. The project owner
# chose Zangband's book titles throughout, over keeping the two town titles,
# knowing this was the cost and that the game is pre-release.
#
# These thirty-five are therefore historical. They are kept because they are the
# only record of the formats this game has written, and because the day a reader
# for them is written -- mapping old book names to new -- this is what would
# prove it worked. They no longer guard against accidental breakage: only the
# fresh characters the suite makes for itself do that now, and a new corpus of
# played characters should replace these.
